Complete the promotion pass: the language's presentational layer is .sp

dan's verdict: "all of it, if we still can write beautifully simple views
that look like an outline" — held: no page source changed a sentence, and
the vitals hold (mean 1.24 args, longest 5).

Eleven more words leave Ruby for lib/vocabulary — figure, disclosure,
empty, text, money, percent, number, badge, time, card, section — over the
atoms the pass grew to carry them:

- `span`, the classed leaf: tag, class and formatting all derive from the
  word; Inference stays in the Generator where it always lived (money,
  percent, number defaults and negative, badge's known-status map, time's
  datetime and moment). Badge's promotion deletes a hatch use.
- `figcaption` (nil-safe) and `summary` (always emitted) — the atoms'
  guards are the old handlers' exact behaviour.
- `region` takes the box's id and open, and BOX_TAGS/BOX_DEPTH carry the
  word's tag and heading depth (a promoted section stays a <section> and
  still deepens).
- A heading inside a box is the box's title: class `#{box}-title` at the
  box's own level — the documented part convention, which reproduces
  `section-title` exactly and quietly normalises `card--title`.
- The preamble grows `parents:`, `speech:`, `subject:`, and three
  situation derivations a page never writes: `empty:` (renders only while
  the enclosing subject is empty — the old guard, and the splice prunes by
  the same flag, the box's own parts untouched), `id:` (the subject's id —
  "no page writes id" survives), `label:` (the app contract's label).
- Compilation's cache read is lock-free (double-checked build), because
  every partial invocation pays it.

Byte-diff over all 13 pages shows exactly three changes, each the law
applying to a word that never owned its box: text, time and disclosure
gained their class — 22 class attributes, hook-only CSS rules. Everything
else — money formatting, badge statuses, section titles, card ids, empty
suppression, heading levels — byte-identical.

Cost re-measured (same instrument): cold 6.95 ms, warm 3.98 ms, 0.17 ms
per partial-in-each row (from 2.75 / 1.37 / 0.10) — the price of every
word being a composition; still payable everywhere.

Stated as atoms, with written verdicts: metric and fact (their bodies are
the app contract), icon (the sprite registry), snippet (chrome). 227 runs /
937 assertions, three checkers 0 problems, 13 pages verified.
